flowchart TD
  classDef works fill:#1d2029,stroke:#555b68,color:#eceef1;
  classDef friction fill:#262a34,stroke:#eceef1,stroke-width:2px,color:#eceef1;
  classDef broken fill:#1d2029,stroke:#d77757,stroke-width:2px,color:#d77757;
  S1["1. The releases page offers tokenpanda-0.1.7.zip<br/>and tokenpanda-0.1.7.zip.sha256.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S2["2. In Terminal, shasum -a 256 -c checks the zip<br/>and prints OK; unzip and move tokenpanda.app to<br/>Applications.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S3["3. With Homebrew instead: brew install<br/>tokenpandadev/tap/tokenpanda, and the caveats<br/>say Open Anyway and Remove before uninstalling.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S4["4. Double click in Applications: macOS refuses,<br/>'Apple could not verify tokenpanda is free of<br/>malware'.<br/><i>friction</i>"]:::friction
  S5["5. System Settings, Privacy and Security, scroll<br/>to the bottom, Open Anyway.<br/><i>friction</i>"]:::friction
  S6["6. The warning comes back once; Open Anyway starts<br/>the app.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S7["7. The first thing the app shows is the<br/>notification permission prompt: nudges are on<br/>by default and the app asks at launch, before<br/>the user has seen it or knows what a nudge is.<br/><i>friction</i>"]:::friction
  S8["8. The menu bar shows the panda alone at half<br/>strength: no figures yet. No window, no Dock<br/>icon.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S9["9. On macOS 26 and later the item stays hidden<br/>until it is allowed in System Settings, Menu<br/>Bar; a crowded menu bar behind the notch hides<br/>it too, and nothing else says the app runs.<br/><i>friction</i>"]:::friction
  S1 --> S2
  S2 --> S3
  S3 --> S4
  S4 --> S5
  S5 --> S6
  S6 --> S7
  S7 --> S8
  S8 --> S9
